//
// Normative rule henvcfg_stce_op (src/priv/hypervisor.adoc):
//   The STCE bit enables vstimecmp for VS-mode when set to one.
//
// Context:
//   VS-mode access also needs menvcfg.STCE=1, mcounteren.TM=1 and hcounteren.TM=1, which the test
//     sets. Enabling means VS-mode CSR instructions on stimecmp operate on vstimecmp, and the
//     vstimecmp comparison drives hip.VSTIP.
//
// Clarifications:
//   https://github.com/riscv/riscv-isa-manual/issues/1985: with menvcfg.STCE=1 and henvcfg.STCE=0,
//     stimecmp accesses from VS and VU raise virtual-instruction exceptions (jhauser-us: "All of
//     the listed cases should raise a virtual-instruction exception").
//   hcounteren bits may be read-only zero (hcounteren_warl). Tests set hcounteren.TM, read it back,
//     and where it reads 0 expect VS-mode accesses to raise virtual-instruction instead.
//
// Test plan:
//   1. henvcfg.STCE=0 then 1: the same VS-mode read of stimecmp raises virtual-instruction, then
//     succeeds.
//   2. With STCE=1, every CSR instruction form on stimecmp in VS-mode returns the old vstimecmp
//     value and leaves the value the form defines; on RV32 also on stimecmph.
//   3. With STCE=1 the comparison drives hip.VSTIP (htimedelta = 0, hvip.VSTIP = 0): vstimecmp = 0
//     gives 1, all ones gives 0.
//   4. Enabling is for VS-mode only: VU-mode reads and writes of stimecmp raise virtual-
//     instruction, with scounteren.TM at 1 and 0.
//   5. Transition: with vstimecmp = 0 and hvip.VSTIP = 0, hip.VSTIP is 0 while henvcfg.STCE=0 and
//     becomes 1 when STCE is set.
//
// Approximate dynamic instruction count: 16211
//

